2025-05-01 02:58:11 - Thread-1097 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns & their potential usage  
• DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS."Id": unique death‑record identifier – join key to the conditions tables.  
• DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS."Age": exact age of decedent – filter 12 through 18 (inclusive).  
• DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS."Race": numeric code for race – join to RACE lookup.  
• DEATH.DEATH.RACE."Code": race code – join to DEATHRECORDS."Race".  
• DEATH.DEATH.RACE."Description": race text – locate descriptions that contain the word ‘black’.  
• DEATH.DEATH.ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS."DeathRecordId": foreign key to DEATHRECORDS."Id".  
• DEATH.DEATH.ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS."Icd10Code": ICD‑10 code present on any entity‑axis line of the death record.  
• DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE."Code": ICD‑10 identifier – join to ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS."Icd10Code".  
• DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE."Description": description of each ICD‑10 code – search for the words ‘vehicle’ or ‘firearm’.  

Key filter conditions that will be used later  
1. DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS."Age" BETWEEN 12 AND 18  
2. DEATH.DEATH.RACE."Description" ILIKE '%black%'  
3. DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'  (or '%firearm%')  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows) that move from simple data peeks to more involved joins which together clarify the values you will ultimately need.

```sql
-- 1) Quick look at ages and race codes for teenagers
SELECT "Id",
       "Age",
       "Race"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS
WHERE "Age" BETWEEN 10 AND 20
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Which race‑lookup rows contain the word “black”?
SELECT DISTINCT "Code",
       "Description"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.RACE
WHERE "Description" ILIKE '%black%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Sample of ICD‑10 codes whose descriptions contain “vehicle”
SELECT "Code",
       "Description"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE
WHERE "Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Entity‑axis rows that reference “vehicle” ICD‑10 codes (joined for the label)
SELECT e."DeathRecordId",
       e."Icd10Code",
       i."Description"
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS  e
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE             i
       ON e."Icd10Code" = i."Code"
WHERE  i."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Entity‑axis rows that reference “firearm” ICD‑10 codes
SELECT e."DeathRecordId",
       e."Icd10Code",
       i."Description"
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS  e
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE             i
       ON e."Icd10Code" = i."Code"
WHERE  i."Description" ILIKE '%firearm%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Total distinct death records that involved any “vehicle” code
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT d."Id")  AS "Vehicle_Death_Count"
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS        d
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS e
       ON d."Id" = e."DeathRecordId"
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE            i
       ON e."Icd10Code" = i."Code"
WHERE  i."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Total distinct death records that involved any “firearm” code
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT d."Id")  AS "Firearm_Death_Count"
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS        d
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS e
       ON d."Id" = e."DeathRecordId"
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE            i
       ON e."Icd10Code" = i."Code"
WHERE  i."Description" ILIKE '%firearm%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Count of ALL deaths by single year of age (12‑18) – no cause filter yet
SELECT d."Age",
       COUNT(DISTINCT d."Id") AS "Total_Deaths"
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS d
WHERE  d."Age" BETWEEN 12 AND 18
GROUP  BY d."Age"
ORDER  BY d."Age"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Count of BLACK deaths by age (12‑18) – still no cause filter
SELECT d."Age",
       COUNT(DISTINCT d."Id") AS "Black_Deaths"
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS d
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.RACE         r
       ON d."Race" = r."Code"
WHERE  d."Age" BETWEEN 12 AND 18
  AND  r."Description" ILIKE '%black%'
GROUP  BY d."Age"
ORDER  BY d."Age"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Prototype of the final combined age / cause / race counts
SELECT d."Age",
       COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN i."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%' THEN d."Id" END)                                         AS "Vehicle_Deaths",
       COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN i."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%' AND r."Description" ILIKE '%black%' THEN d."Id" END)      AS "Black_Vehicle_Deaths",
       COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN i."Description" ILIKE '%firearm%' THEN d."Id" END)                                         AS "Firearm_Deaths",
       COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN i."Description" ILIKE '%firearm%' AND r."Description" ILIKE '%black%' THEN d."Id" END)      AS "Black_Firearm_Deaths"
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS         d
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS e
       ON d."Id" = e."DeathRecordId"
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE            i
       ON e."Icd10Code" = i."Code"
LEFT  JOIN DEATH.DEATH.RACE             r
       ON d."Race" = r."Code"
WHERE  d."Age" BETWEEN 12 AND 18
GROUP  BY d."Age"
ORDER  BY d."Age"
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries take you from inspecting lookup values (“black”, “vehicle”, “firearm”) through progressively richer joins, culminating in a single statement that produces, for every age 12‑18, the counts you ultimately need (total, and Black‑only, for both cause groups).
